erious character  who we saw following adam that day in  the black vehicle  and he also saw him taking pictures of  the crime scene and we'll see  that i would assume this black car took  the picture of him  or video at the gas station he sends to  michael  at the end of this episode but i love  the turn of michael's character here  when he goes to see the black male he  doesn't have the money and he says i  don't think you have the evidence  to pull this off or the balls to see  this through i have to say i know people  get annoyed every time i mention  breaking bad but come on it reminds me  of walter white that's why i love seeing  it but  it's just like something he would do i  have to acknowledge that it's there you  see it if you watch breaking bad it just  comes back to you but it ended really  strong this episode  having now jimmy baxter figure out  oh my god this judge knows who killed my  son and  this is a catalyst now to make me feel  like episode 6 is going to be  crazy and that we got this blackmailer  involved  and michael's just got all these things  happening that are a result of his  decision to cover up what happened with  adam everything is breaking everyone's  getting onto him you got lee  also catching on more and more to what  really happened to kofi so  i'm excited to see how this all plays  out this got me a lot more interested  again  it was a good setup episode for which  should be a crazy episode six calming  down a bit  from the blow up in last episode's  cliffhanger but now setting to this big  moment at the mid point of the season  that jimmy baxter  now is on to michael so in general it's  a stronger episode this season i'm  actually going to give this one an 8.5  and the only reason i don't give it a  little higher is because i still felt  like  the way it was presented timeline wise  was confusing it's not that i didn't get  where we were but it was  hard task almost too hard it they made  it over complicated and  where people were 